WEBVTT

01:20.372 --> 01:21.539
Bullshit.

01:21.540 --> 01:23.749
It is this friggin' wide.

01:23.750 --> 01:25.251
And it's periodic.

01:25.252 --> 01:27.628
Bull. Shit.

01:27.629 --> 01:28.714
Show me.

01:35.429 --> 01:37.014
Something terrestrial, gotta be.

01:37.890 --> 01:39.348
Bouncing off the moon.

01:39.349 --> 01:41.685
Gee. I never thought to check that.

01:42.394 --> 01:44.103
Look at that slope, man.

01:44.104 --> 01:46.022
You could ski down that thing.

01:46.023 --> 01:47.398
It is drifting.

01:47.399 --> 01:50.234
Look here. Zoom in. Zoom in.

01:50.235 --> 01:51.570
See that variation?

01:52.070 --> 01:55.489
And look. This gap here?
This is where it stops, then starts over.

01:55.490 --> 01:58.117
- It repeats?
- Every 78 seconds.

01:58.118 --> 01:59.494
The whole entire thing.

02:00.495 --> 02:02.831
Three hours straight, and no end in sight.

02:07.169 --> 02:08.169
It can't be.

02:20.474 --> 02:22.808
It's gotta be something
bouncing off the... off the...

02:22.809 --> 02:24.977
It's not bouncing off the moon, Dave.

02:24.978 --> 02:28.065
Well, maybe it's those Chatty Cathys
at the Forest Service.

02:28.857 --> 02:31.442
I hate those guys. Always on their radios,
talking about trees.

02:31.443 --> 02:33.528
Dave, it's not Smokey Bear
we're picking up.

02:33.529 --> 02:34.613
Look at that signal.

02:35.113 --> 02:36.198
It's drifting.

02:37.407 --> 02:38.492
What is it, then?

02:45.040 --> 02:48.210
Looks like simple pulse-width modulation.
Old-school, like Morse code.

02:49.253 --> 02:53.172
Maybe somehow,
it's the time signal out of Fort Collins.

02:53.173 --> 02:56.008
- They use pulse-width modulation.
- It's not the atomic clock.

02:56.009 --> 02:58.511
The atomic clock changes every minute
because it's a clock.

02:58.512 --> 03:01.430
This is the same exact data
repeated every 78 seconds.

03:01.431 --> 03:06.645
Plus, this is coming
from 600 light-years away.

03:08.939 --> 03:12.150
This Morse code of yours
seems to be split four ways.

03:15.362 --> 03:17.405
The pulses are of equal duration,

03:17.406 --> 03:20.241
but they're positioned
across four different frequencies.

03:20.242 --> 03:23.579
- Looks like a player piano.
- So not binary but base four.

03:24.079 --> 03:25.080
Quaternary.

03:26.832 --> 03:28.333
This won't be easy to crack.

03:36.091 --> 03:37.718
No, no. If you look at this. Look at...

03:40.304 --> 03:41.429
What do you think it says?

03:41.430 --> 03:45.017
Maybe just,
"Hello. Hey, hey. We're out here."

03:45.517 --> 03:48.687
What did we put on Voyagers 1 and 2?
Chuck Berry?

03:49.229 --> 03:51.899
Maybe this is just
their version of "Johnny B. Goode."

03:53.775 --> 03:56.069
Imagine the power it took to send it.

03:56.904 --> 03:57.905
Megawatts?

03:58.655 --> 03:59.823
Gigawatts?

04:00.699 --> 04:02.825
And that's if it's pointed only at us.

04:02.826 --> 04:04.619
Antenna the size of Africa.

04:04.620 --> 04:05.704
Bigger.

04:07.789 --> 04:10.167
You go to all that trouble
to send a message,

04:10.959 --> 04:12.878
it's gotta be more than just "hello."

04:14.505 --> 04:16.839
And why make it hard to understand?

04:17.423 --> 04:18.466
Quaternary?

04:19.091 --> 04:21.553
That's like encryption.
Why would you bother to...

04:30.729 --> 04:32.105
It's not quaternary.

04:36.443 --> 04:38.070
I think I know what it is.

05:21.446 --> 05:23.948
The twin moons hung low and full.

05:23.949 --> 05:26.784
Two wine-green eyes
peering over the horizon

05:26.785 --> 05:29.204
as if to steal a glimpse
into Lucasia's soul.

05:29.955 --> 05:32.123
She paced the blood-soaked decks
of the Mercator,

05:32.124 --> 05:36.003
looking for something, anything,
that might take her mind off Raban.

05:36.962 --> 05:40.841
Ascending the forecastle, her gaze
lingered over a bare-chested young sailor.

05:41.466 --> 05:43.301
On hands and knees he scrubbed,

05:43.302 --> 05:47.723
his sinewy forearms stretched taut as he
washed away all trace of the day's fight.

05:48.432 --> 05:50.142
With a languid nod...

05:51.977 --> 05:54.479
Lucasia bade him follow to her cabin.

05:54.980 --> 05:58.357
Little did this callow deckhand know
that serving at his captain's pleasure

05:58.358 --> 06:00.194
might take on such sweet meaning.

06:01.445 --> 06:05.449
Or, regrettably,
that it would last but a single night.

06:08.285 --> 06:12.788
Later, at four bells,
Lucasia stood by the mizzenmast.

06:12.789 --> 06:15.959
Once again, she was alone.

06:17.085 --> 06:18.794
She pulled her topcoat tighter,

06:18.795 --> 06:21.923
fingering its coarse wool
as her thoughts flashed back to Raban.

06:21.924 --> 06:25.259
It had been he who first wrapped
the coat around her,

06:25.260 --> 06:27.136
whispering in her ear,

06:27.137 --> 06:31.600
"May this keep you warm
in my absence, ma chérie."

06:33.185 --> 06:37.064
With that, Raban, proud, haughty Raban,

06:37.981 --> 06:40.192
mounted the plank and leaped from sight.

06:40.776 --> 06:43.278
The amaranthine slipsand closed over him,

06:44.571 --> 06:45.906
leaving nary a ripple.

06:58.085 --> 07:02.213
Attention, lovers of speculative
historical romance literature,

07:02.214 --> 07:05.925
best-selling author Carol Sturka
will now sign her new novel,

07:05.926 --> 07:07.510
"Bloodsong of Wycaro,"

07:07.511 --> 07:09.762
the fourth book in her
"Winds of Wycaro" trilogy.

07:09.763 --> 07:12.724
"Why-car-oh," please!
It's "Winds of Why-car-oh!"

07:13.892 --> 07:16.060
And Bloodsong is the best yet.

07:16.061 --> 07:17.813
God, are you in for a treat.

07:19.356 --> 07:20.691
Let's go sign books!

07:23.652 --> 07:25.903
Raban is alive, right?

07:25.904 --> 07:27.864
Maureen. You could read it.

07:27.865 --> 07:29.282
Well, I will. Tonight.

07:29.283 --> 07:31.409
I've already unplugged the phone.

07:31.410 --> 07:33.077
Just...

07:33.078 --> 07:35.621
- Raban's not on the cover.
- No, he's not.

07:35.622 --> 07:39.042
And he's never not been
on the cover, Carol.

07:39.585 --> 07:41.295
If Raban doesn't come back...

07:42.421 --> 07:43.422
I'm done.

07:44.173 --> 07:45.174
Come here.

07:46.175 --> 07:48.051
Page 218.

07:51.263 --> 07:53.764
- Okay. Thank you.
- Okay. Bye.

07:53.765 --> 07:54.932
Thanks, Maureen.

07:54.933 --> 07:57.686
- Okay, this is Olga.
- Hi. Hi, Olga.

08:01.440 --> 08:02.441
Hi, Yvette!

08:04.026 --> 08:05.319
Hi!

08:05.944 --> 08:06.987
Love it.

08:08.155 --> 08:11.157
- Happy reading.
- This is Nicky, with a pillow.

08:11.158 --> 08:13.284
- Nicky with a... Oh, my gosh!
- I made it myself.

08:13.285 --> 08:15.119
- Look at that. You made this?
- Yes.

08:15.120 --> 08:16.204
This is Christine.

08:16.205 --> 08:18.372
This is Paulina and support person.

08:18.373 --> 08:19.540
- This is Carlotta.
- Hi.

08:19.541 --> 08:21.250
Say, "Raban".

08:21.251 --> 08:23.002
Raban.

08:23.003 --> 08:25.421
When Raban and Eldgammel
fell in the cargo hold,

08:25.422 --> 08:27.381
do you remember what it was loaded with?

08:27.382 --> 08:28.674
Mandovian spicefruit.

08:28.675 --> 08:30.844
Which Lucasia is...

08:32.179 --> 08:33.803
Deathly allergic to!

08:33.804 --> 08:36.265
- You guys run a fan club?
- Of course!

08:38.977 --> 08:40.478
- Thank you so much!
- Thank you.

08:40.479 --> 08:41.562
- Hi, Tanya.
- Hi!

08:41.563 --> 08:42.772
- Are you excited?
- Yes.

08:42.773 --> 08:44.065
- Hi, Yvonne.
- Hi.

08:44.066 --> 08:45.983
I got two books, one for the tub.

08:45.984 --> 08:49.028
This is a authentic cutlass
just like Raban's.

08:49.029 --> 08:50.780
- Okay.
- Careful, it's really sharp.

08:50.781 --> 08:52.365
Okay, so three things.

08:52.366 --> 08:55.660
A: When finally are they
gonna make a "Wycaro" movie?

08:55.661 --> 08:58.663
And please tell me it'll be in actual
theaters, not on the Lifetime Network.

08:58.664 --> 09:00.998
B: You gotta get ILM to do the slipsand,

09:00.999 --> 09:03.543
otherwise it's just gonna look like merde,
pardon my French.

09:03.544 --> 09:07.213
And C: A small but very crucial point,

09:07.214 --> 09:12.051
as a two-masted schooner, the Mercator
would not possess a mizzenmast. So...

09:12.052 --> 09:14.887
Craig, I'm gonna need you
to put this back in the bag

09:14.888 --> 09:16.473
before the store manager sees it.

09:17.432 --> 09:18.432
Right.

09:18.433 --> 09:19.852
- Your humble servant.
- Thank you.

09:21.478 --> 09:22.771
That's the one.

09:23.730 --> 09:25.023
Thank you so much.

09:25.691 --> 09:27.692
- We'll see you at the next one.
- Happy reading.

09:27.693 --> 09:29.570
All right. All right.

09:33.699 --> 09:37.243
Hi, ladies. I have us
going to the Hyatt Regency Dallas.

09:37.244 --> 09:39.580
Hi. Yeah. Thanks, perfect.

09:40.163 --> 09:43.834
That was quite a send-off.
I'm sorry, should I know who you are?

09:45.335 --> 09:47.171
Depends. You a big fan of mindless crap?

10:21.079 --> 10:22.330
Morning, Doc.

10:22.331 --> 10:24.458
Well, it certainly is.

10:25.584 --> 10:27.127
- Hey, Mel.
- Hey.

10:27.920 --> 10:29.254
Where'd those come from?

10:29.838 --> 10:30.839
Yours truly.

10:31.507 --> 10:33.674
Help yourself.
I think they're mostly glazed,

10:33.675 --> 10:36.761
but one box ought to be sprinkled,
powdered and all that.

10:36.762 --> 10:38.555
What did we do to deserve this?

10:39.556 --> 10:41.934
My 14-year-old's selling 'em
for marching band.

10:43.393 --> 10:44.602
Well, aren't you a good dad.

10:44.603 --> 10:46.897
- What does she play?
- Trombone.

10:47.981 --> 10:52.360
- Doctor D!
- Good evening. Morning. Whatever.

10:52.361 --> 10:54.654
- Look what Mel brought.
- For us?

10:54.655 --> 10:55.905
Yeah, please.

10:55.906 --> 10:57.698
They got you two working late.

10:57.699 --> 11:00.118
Yeah. I gotta gas a bunch of rats.

11:01.286 --> 11:02.829
So, how goes the big project?

11:03.497 --> 11:04.540
What have you heard?

11:05.249 --> 11:07.125
I don't know. Things.

11:07.668 --> 11:09.169
Well...

11:09.837 --> 11:11.420
Our team's fairly certain
we've got a sequence

11:11.421 --> 11:13.005
that encodes for a lysogenic virus.

11:13.006 --> 11:14.924
But after eight whole months
of animal testing...

11:14.925 --> 11:16.843
Macaques, rabbits, mice...

11:16.844 --> 11:19.471
- Guinea pigs.
- Guinea pigs. Now rats.

11:19.972 --> 11:22.057
No clinical signs whatsoever.

11:24.560 --> 11:25.769
Put another way...

11:26.603 --> 11:27.604
we got bubkes.

11:28.438 --> 11:29.523
We got bubkes.

11:45.163 --> 11:46.748
Okay, how do you wanna do this?

11:47.666 --> 11:50.586
I can put 'em to sleep
if you wanna do the cardiac sticks.

11:51.461 --> 11:53.671
I hate the cardiac sticks.

11:53.672 --> 11:55.924
Well, you're more than welcome
to gas them.

11:56.550 --> 11:58.009
I hate gassing them.

11:58.010 --> 11:59.886
Might be in the wrong career.

11:59.887 --> 12:02.472
All right, cardiac sticks it is.

12:03.515 --> 12:04.725
Let's get it over with.

12:09.605 --> 12:10.606
Check it out.

12:11.273 --> 12:12.399
Damn.

12:13.525 --> 12:15.235
What do you figure happened there?

12:21.325 --> 12:22.367
I don't know.

12:45.140 --> 12:46.600
He's looking pretty dead to me.

12:49.102 --> 12:50.102
You got a heartbeat?

12:50.103 --> 12:52.022
I can't feel jack shit in these gloves.

13:01.657 --> 13:02.783
Huh, what?

13:04.159 --> 13:05.576
He's absolutely got a heartbeat.

13:05.577 --> 13:07.703
A strong one. Just bam, bam, bam.

13:07.704 --> 13:09.456
It's weird.
If I didn't know any better, I'd...

13:10.040 --> 13:11.999
God. Oh, shit. Oh, no.

13:12.000 --> 13:13.710
You've got to be kidding me.

13:15.128 --> 13:17.005
- Shit.
- Did he break the skin?

13:17.673 --> 13:19.924
Yeah, I don't...
Yeah, it's through the glove.

13:19.925 --> 13:22.134
Shit. Soak it quick.

13:22.135 --> 13:23.219
Keep it submerged.

13:23.220 --> 13:25.680
If it's bleeding,
make sure to squeeze it out good.

13:25.681 --> 13:28.642
I'm gonna call this in
as soon as I catch him, okay?

13:45.492 --> 13:46.743
Right there.

13:52.291 --> 13:54.960
Let's mark 3:36 and...

13:57.880 --> 13:59.173
Jenn?

14:02.259 --> 14:03.968
Talk to me, Jenn. Jenn!

14:03.969 --> 14:05.929
Jenn! Jenn! Jenn!

14:06.972 --> 14:08.307
We are getting out right now.

14:09.808 --> 14:12.060
I got you. Okay, come on.

14:12.936 --> 14:13.979
I got you.

14:20.027 --> 14:21.028
Hang on.

14:22.696 --> 14:24.864
Jenn, can you hear me? It's gonna be fine.

14:24.865 --> 14:25.949
You're gonna be all right.

14:27.826 --> 14:31.287
Come on. You're gonna be all right.
You're gonna be all right, you hear me?

14:31.288 --> 14:34.248
Come on, come on, come on.
Talk to me. Come on, Jenn, come on.

14:34.249 --> 14:36.210
Jenn! You all right?

14:37.461 --> 14:38.462
Jenn?

14:39.004 --> 14:40.047
Just say something.

14:40.756 --> 14:42.423
Jenn. I got you.

14:42.424 --> 14:43.509
I got you.

14:44.218 --> 14:45.219
Jenn?

14:47.387 --> 14:49.348
Hey, hey, hey, Jenn. Can you hear me?

14:50.599 --> 14:51.767
Jenn, say something.

15:02.194 --> 15:03.195
Damn it.

15:04.279 --> 15:05.280
Kidding me?

15:18.460 --> 15:19.461
Really?

15:28.011 --> 15:29.012
Damn.

15:32.850 --> 15:34.393
Can you believe this thing?

15:36.353 --> 15:39.523
You've got skinny arms.
Do you think you could maybe...

15:42.901 --> 15:43.902
Hey.

16:25.903 --> 16:26.904
Yes?

19:27.459 --> 19:28.627
I'm gonna get some gum.

20:10.836 --> 20:11.836
Seriously?

20:11.837 --> 20:15.299
I had one Tito's in Salt Lake.
That was, like, two hours ago.

20:39.156 --> 20:40.282
Rye Manhattan...

20:42.284 --> 20:44.076
and a Diet Pepsi.

20:44.077 --> 20:45.162
Thanks.

20:48.290 --> 20:49.750
We could take a cab home.

20:50.417 --> 20:52.752
Don't tell me you don't need a drink,
'cause you need a drink.

20:52.753 --> 20:55.046
- I don't need a drink.
- You need a drink.

20:55.047 --> 20:56.255
I don't need a drink.

20:56.256 --> 20:57.966
I call bullshit on that.

20:58.550 --> 21:00.093
I need sleep, that's what I need.

21:00.677 --> 21:02.971
Hey, cheers, to the best tour yet.

21:04.765 --> 21:06.849
- You gonna leave me hanging here?
- I do not clink glasses

21:06.850 --> 21:08.518
with fucking Diet Pepsi.

21:08.519 --> 21:11.145
Best book tour? What is that?

21:11.146 --> 21:12.773
Is that like best stomach cancer?

21:13.315 --> 21:14.899
You endure it, you do not toast it.

21:14.900 --> 21:18.945
How I hate all those paying customers
showering me with love and respect.

21:18.946 --> 21:20.781
And why do I have to make so much money?

21:22.282 --> 21:23.492
How do you bear it?

21:32.835 --> 21:33.918
Bunch of dummies.

21:33.919 --> 21:38.006
Wow. It's a ship that sails on... sand?

21:38.632 --> 21:41.300
Purple sand? That is... That's brilliant.

21:41.301 --> 21:42.469
The world needed that.

21:43.220 --> 21:45.221
And the world needed
yet another female character

21:45.222 --> 21:49.518
who spends all her time mooning over
some fucking proud and haughty pirate.

21:50.143 --> 21:51.770
He's a corsair, not a pirate.

21:53.564 --> 21:55.065
"Mandovian spicefruit."

21:56.608 --> 21:57.942
Jesus. That... I...

21:57.943 --> 21:59.944
It's like a bad episode of Star Trek.

21:59.945 --> 22:01.697
So how about
you throw everybody a changeup?

22:02.447 --> 22:03.949
Green sand instead of purple?

22:05.242 --> 22:06.994
Maybe it's time for your serious book.

22:09.162 --> 22:11.915
Why not? You've been plugging away
at it for five years.

22:12.416 --> 22:14.584
- Four and a half. Barely.
- Pardon me.

22:14.585 --> 22:15.751
So put it out already.

22:15.752 --> 22:17.045
I can't just... It...

22:18.547 --> 22:19.756
It needs polishing.

22:21.175 --> 22:22.758
Obviously. I mean it does, right?

22:22.759 --> 22:25.052
Okay, take the next few months and polish.

22:25.053 --> 22:26.137
I'll work it out.

22:26.138 --> 22:28.432
I'll buy you some more time
before your next Wycaro.

22:30.475 --> 22:32.853
You really think
Bitter Chrysalis is that good?

22:35.147 --> 22:36.773
I think people will love it.

22:42.654 --> 22:44.822
You ever read Finnegans Wake?

22:44.823 --> 22:45.908
No.

22:46.617 --> 22:48.911
I tried to. In grad school.

22:51.538 --> 22:54.166
It's probably great. I don't know.

22:55.918 --> 22:58.712
All I know is it made me miserable
trying to get through it.

23:01.965 --> 23:02.966
I figure...

23:04.176 --> 23:07.095
you make even one person happy,
maybe that's not art.

23:09.348 --> 23:10.557
But it's something.

23:17.648 --> 23:18.649
To Raban.

23:19.566 --> 23:21.985
Proud, haughty Raban.

23:29.743 --> 23:31.245
Did you bring your cigarettes?

23:31.995 --> 23:33.288
Since when do you smoke?

23:34.081 --> 23:35.165
Since now.

23:56.186 --> 23:59.147
Are you trying to start a forest fire?
Stop wasting my butane.

24:00.983 --> 24:02.733
Stop telling me how to smoke.

24:02.734 --> 24:03.943
I used to smoke in middle school.

24:03.944 --> 24:06.404
You're supposed to light the other
person's cigarette first, by the way.

24:06.405 --> 24:07.989
- That's etiquette.
- Yeah? On a plane,

24:07.990 --> 24:10.075
do you put your own oxygen mask on first?

24:14.830 --> 24:17.624
Do you wanna hear what HoustonMom78
says about Bloodsong?

24:18.250 --> 24:20.459
"Best Wycaro ever!" All caps.

24:20.460 --> 24:21.545
And...

24:23.589 --> 24:26.507
- 16, 17 exclamation points.
- Wow.

24:26.508 --> 24:27.842
- Is that a new record?
- It's gotta be.

24:27.843 --> 24:31.429
"Spoiler alert, Raban is back
and yummier that ever."

24:31.430 --> 24:33.599
Yummier than ever, I think she means.

24:34.474 --> 24:37.894
"You better belief
he's got my permission to come aboard.

24:37.895 --> 24:39.395
I'd walk his plank any time."

24:39.396 --> 24:40.897
I'm sensing a nautical motif.

24:40.898 --> 24:43.232
A little bit. Think HoustonMom's
off her meds again?

24:43.233 --> 24:45.861
I think HoustonMom would spread her legs
for a grilled cheese sandwich.

24:51.491 --> 24:52.492
Look at that.

24:53.785 --> 24:55.161
What?

24:55.162 --> 24:56.872
What do you think they're doing?

24:57.664 --> 25:00.792
- What's what doing?
- The planes. Up. Look.

25:03.378 --> 25:05.630
I don't know. What, is that weird?

25:05.631 --> 25:07.131
Yeah, it's weird. Isn't it?

25:07.132 --> 25:09.593
All of them kinda parallel like that.

25:22.814 --> 25:24.316
Anybody else weigh in?

25:25.025 --> 25:27.861
It's all the usual suspects,
plus a few new ones.

25:28.445 --> 25:29.488
Everybody loves it.

25:40.958 --> 25:42.668
You wanna answer a few questions for them?

25:43.794 --> 25:45.628
- What, now? No. No, no.
- Do one quick one.

25:45.629 --> 25:47.589
Let 'em know you're paying attention.

25:48.590 --> 25:51.425
"Carol, my husband says
Raban can be my hall pass,

25:51.426 --> 25:54.262
which I don't think is fair
since Raban's not a real-life person,

25:54.263 --> 25:55.805
although I wish he was.

25:55.806 --> 25:59.725
In real-life, was there an actual man
you were thinking of

25:59.726 --> 26:01.519
when you came up with Raban?"

26:01.520 --> 26:02.896
That's hilarious.

26:05.983 --> 26:07.192
You wanna tell her the truth?

26:09.778 --> 26:10.988
What do you have to lose?

26:14.074 --> 26:15.200
Put down George Clooney.

26:16.034 --> 26:17.076
- What?
- Nothing.

26:17.077 --> 26:18.870
- What's wrong with him?
- Nothing. Just...

26:18.871 --> 26:21.080
I mean, how about
a hot Brazilian soccer player?

26:21.081 --> 26:22.749
Someone with dreadlocks. Hip it up.

26:24.084 --> 26:25.085
Just...

26:26.170 --> 26:27.296
put George Clooney.

26:28.130 --> 26:29.131
It's safer.

26:34.344 --> 26:35.721
Shit.

26:57.075 --> 26:59.244
Buddy, you... You okay, buddy?

27:05.834 --> 27:06.919
Jesus.

27:17.804 --> 27:19.640
Helen, should we call someone?

27:22.351 --> 27:23.434
Helen?

27:23.435 --> 27:25.270
Helen, stop looking at the goddamn...

27:37.908 --> 27:38.909
Helen?

27:43.121 --> 27:44.289
Oh, my God. Helen!

27:45.082 --> 27:46.083
Helen?

27:47.125 --> 27:48.168
Helen?

27:51.672 --> 27:52.797
Help!

27:52.798 --> 27:54.715
Somebody help us!

27:54.716 --> 27:56.008
Help!

27:56.009 --> 27:58.846
Just hang in there. Hang in there.

27:59.388 --> 28:00.639
Just hang in there.

28:07.813 --> 28:09.147
Call 911...

28:18.031 --> 28:19.366
Oh, God.

29:22.554 --> 29:24.138
Come on, please.

29:24.139 --> 29:25.307
Please, please.

29:27.768 --> 29:29.685
- You've reached the Albuquerque Police...
- Yes. Hi. I...

29:29.686 --> 29:31.020
- ...emergency number.
- Shit!

29:31.021 --> 29:32.563
- Please remain on the line.
- Fuck!

29:32.564 --> 29:34.775
- An operator will be with you shortly.
- Fuck!

29:35.359 --> 29:37.486
You've reached the Albuquerque Police...

30:20.904 --> 30:26.410
Come on, come on, come on.

30:27.995 --> 30:29.246
Come on, come on, come on!

30:34.001 --> 30:35.127
Fuck you.

30:35.669 --> 30:38.422
Fuck you. Fuck you. Fuck you.

30:42.676 --> 30:43.677
Fuck you!

30:52.227 --> 30:55.898
Hey, you gotta get out.
Come on, get out. Get out! Oh, God.

30:59.776 --> 31:01.445
No! Fuck!

31:04.198 --> 31:05.532
Fucking go!

32:32.911 --> 32:33.912
Thank God.

32:36.123 --> 32:37.541
Thank God.

33:57.538 --> 33:59.206
Hey. Hey.

34:01.291 --> 34:02.292
Wake up.

34:05.003 --> 34:08.257
Dr. Nguyen, I need you to wake up.

34:09.257 --> 34:10.800
Please wake up.

34:10.801 --> 34:11.885
Doctor.

34:12.469 --> 34:13.637
Dr. Nguyen, wake up.

34:14.221 --> 34:15.222
Wake up.

34:15.806 --> 34:16.849
Please wake up.

34:17.850 --> 34:19.560
Dr. Nguyen, wake up!

34:23.563 --> 34:24.565
Okay.

34:55.053 --> 34:56.388
I'm so sorry! Fuck.

35:00.809 --> 35:02.186
Okay.

35:20.829 --> 35:22.456
Okay. Here we go.

35:25.667 --> 35:26.752
Helen?

35:27.711 --> 35:29.004
Helen? Helen?

35:32.007 --> 35:33.759
Helen. Helen.

35:38.013 --> 35:39.014
Hi.

35:40.224 --> 35:41.433
Baby.

35:48.190 --> 35:49.608
Hi, baby.

35:56.198 --> 35:57.366
No, no, no.

36:24.351 --> 36:25.519
Goddamn it.

36:26.645 --> 36:27.646
Okay.

36:32.025 --> 36:33.235
Come on.

36:36.697 --> 36:39.198
Somebody please help me.

36:39.199 --> 36:41.909
No, no, no. God, no. Don't...

36:41.910 --> 36:44.496
Please. Please.

38:17.047 --> 38:18.048
Hey.

38:21.176 --> 38:22.261
Hey.

38:30.894 --> 38:32.771
What is happening?

38:49.288 --> 38:50.997
Hey! Hey! Don't you touch her!

38:50.998 --> 38:53.416
You put her down. Put her down.

38:53.417 --> 38:55.294
Get out! Go away!

38:59.756 --> 39:02.301
What the hell is wrong with you people?

39:03.010 --> 39:05.345
We just wanna help, Carol.

40:14.748 --> 40:17.125
What the fuck?

42:29.383 --> 42:30.509
Christ, no.

42:48.235 --> 42:49.569
Come on, come on, come on.

42:49.570 --> 42:51.446
Come on, come on, please.

43:06.461 --> 43:07.838
There's a spare key.

43:10.299 --> 43:11.508
We can show you.

43:12.009 --> 43:15.094
No. No, stop. Don't come any closer.

43:15.095 --> 43:17.096
We don't mean to scare you, Carol.

43:17.097 --> 43:18.556
You're in no danger.

43:18.557 --> 43:20.434
We really do want to help.

43:20.934 --> 43:23.477
Remember? April 2016.

43:23.478 --> 43:25.355
The last time you got locked out.

43:26.023 --> 43:28.025
You put a spare key under the flower pot.

43:29.109 --> 43:30.235
The one on the right.

43:31.069 --> 43:32.070
Back there.

43:38.869 --> 43:39.870
There you go.

43:46.960 --> 43:48.170
Leave me alone.

43:49.087 --> 43:50.796
- Please.
- Sure, Carol.

43:50.797 --> 43:53.258
Just give us a couple of minutes
to clear out.

44:31.213 --> 44:33.340
We're very sorry for your loss.

47:03.907 --> 47:04.908
Fuck yeah!

47:06.076 --> 47:07.286
God bless America.

48:46.760 --> 48:49.513
Hi, Carol. Thank you for calling.

48:54.142 --> 48:55.143
Yep.

48:55.644 --> 48:57.937
This must be so bewildering for you.

48:57.938 --> 48:59.105
So terrible.

48:59.106 --> 49:01.775
All the death and destruction
you witnessed tonight.

49:02.401 --> 49:06.571
Especially Helen's passing.
Please know none of that was intentional.

49:06.572 --> 49:08.824
You have our deepest condolences.

49:09.324 --> 49:11.784
And to say it again, you are in no danger.

49:11.785 --> 49:13.620
You are perfectly safe.

49:14.663 --> 49:16.707
- Okay.
- Your life is your own.

49:17.541 --> 49:18.916
Please know that.

49:18.917 --> 49:21.712
Your well-being
is of utmost importance to us.

49:22.337 --> 49:23.338
Okay.

49:24.214 --> 49:25.548
Completely up to you, of course,

49:25.549 --> 49:28.801
but you might want to stick close to home
for the next few days.

49:28.802 --> 49:32.763
We've a lot to clean up,
and it may be distressing for you to see.

49:32.764 --> 49:35.600
But we will put things right.

49:35.601 --> 49:39.478
To that end, if we may be of assistance
with Helen's remains...

49:39.479 --> 49:40.939
- Nope.
- Okay.

49:41.607 --> 49:43.983
If we can help you in any way
please let us know.

49:43.984 --> 49:48.404
We can deliver food, medicine,
whatever you need.

49:48.405 --> 49:50.406
Just dial zero, day or night.

49:50.407 --> 49:54.827
You will want to call from a landline
as all the cellular networks are down.

49:54.828 --> 49:56.872
But we are here for you.

50:00.876 --> 50:03.962
We feel like we're doing
all the talking here.

50:05.088 --> 50:07.590
Are there any questions
you might have for us, Carol?

50:07.591 --> 50:08.800
Anything at all.

50:14.306 --> 50:16.475
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

50:17.893 --> 50:19.520
I guess to start with,

50:20.354 --> 50:23.814
what the fuck is happening?

50:23.815 --> 50:25.274
Well, basically...

50:25.275 --> 50:26.776
It's an alien invasion, right?

50:26.777 --> 50:28.694
I mean, obviously it's an alien invasion.

50:28.695 --> 50:30.154
Actually, no. It is not.

50:30.155 --> 50:33.032
What the fuck it isn't. You know my name.

50:33.033 --> 50:35.576
You know Helen's name.

50:35.577 --> 50:39.248
You are talking to me from my TV!

50:39.831 --> 50:43.167
And what the fuck is with everybody's...

50:43.168 --> 50:44.544
Shit like this...

50:44.545 --> 50:48.297
And those two weird...
the weird neighbor kids next door.

50:48.298 --> 50:49.842
They know where some goddamn key...

50:50.425 --> 50:53.678
How would they know that, huh?

50:53.679 --> 50:57.181
- Are you reading my mind?
- No. Absolutely not.

50:57.182 --> 50:58.933
We couldn't do that if we wanted to.

50:58.934 --> 51:01.561
Who is "we?"
Why is everybody suddenly "we?"

51:01.562 --> 51:04.522
You know, we could continue this
after you've had a good night's sleep.

51:04.523 --> 51:06.691
Who is "we?"

51:06.692 --> 51:08.985
"We" is us. Just us.

51:08.986 --> 51:10.069
Who the fuck is "us?"

51:10.070 --> 51:12.948
Us. There are no aliens.

51:13.615 --> 51:15.074
Not on this planet.

51:15.075 --> 51:20.413
We are, however, beneficiaries
of extraterrestrial technology.

51:20.414 --> 51:23.291
Fourteen months ago,
astronomers discovered a radio signal

51:23.292 --> 51:25.669
from 600 light-years away.

51:26.253 --> 51:27.879
There's no telling
how long it's been repeating.

51:27.880 --> 51:30.591
Maybe throughout all of human existence.

51:31.300 --> 51:34.302
This signal, it's made up of four tones

51:34.303 --> 51:39.349
representing guanine, uracil,
adenine and cytosine.

51:40.058 --> 51:43.437
It's a recipe, it turns out,
for a nucleotide sequence.

51:44.021 --> 51:45.147
RNA.

51:46.148 --> 51:48.858
Scientists have created
this sequence in a lab.

51:48.859 --> 51:53.863
It is not a living thing, per se.
It is more akin to a virus.

51:53.864 --> 51:55.824
Though it's not that exactly either.

51:56.909 --> 52:01.246
It's kind of a psychic glue
capable of binding us all together.

52:03.165 --> 52:04.166
Okay.

52:05.459 --> 52:06.877
So, if you're not aliens...

52:08.837 --> 52:10.464
Who am I talking to right now?
Who are you?

52:11.340 --> 52:13.257
This particular individual?

52:13.258 --> 52:14.967
This is Davis Taffler.

52:14.968 --> 52:19.389
Under Secretary of Agriculture
for Farm Production and Conservation.

52:20.265 --> 52:23.935
But you are currently
talking to every person on Earth,

52:23.936 --> 52:25.771
including Davis Taffler.

52:26.396 --> 52:27.397
We're all one.

52:27.981 --> 52:29.274
How does that work?

52:30.025 --> 52:32.653
We don't know exactly. It just does.

52:34.571 --> 52:35.947
Can I talk to the President?

52:35.948 --> 52:39.033
That individual passed away this evening,
unfortunately.

52:39.034 --> 52:43.329
Along with quite a few senior members
of the United States government.

52:43.330 --> 52:48.334
Davis Taffler happened to be
nearby and intact.

52:48.335 --> 52:49.961
And he was wearing a suit. So...

52:49.962 --> 52:52.630
So, you're in charge now?

52:52.631 --> 52:54.465
- The Under Secretary of...
- No.

52:54.466 --> 52:57.511
Nobody's in charge.
Or everybody's in charge.

52:58.095 --> 52:59.887
Really, there's no such thing anymore.

52:59.888 --> 53:02.890
But there's got to be others like me.

53:02.891 --> 53:05.309
Your situation is a rare one.

53:05.310 --> 53:08.646
There appear to be
11 other individuals like yourself.

53:08.647 --> 53:10.106
In Albuquerque?

53:10.107 --> 53:12.317
No. In the world.

53:12.818 --> 53:14.236
We have reached out to them.

53:14.736 --> 53:17.948
Like you, they are disoriented.
Understandably.

53:19.825 --> 53:21.367
Rest assured, Carol.

53:21.368 --> 53:24.162
We will figure out
what makes you different.

53:25.038 --> 53:26.123
Figure it out why?

53:26.790 --> 53:28.041
So we can fix it.

53:29.042 --> 53:30.669
So you can join us.

53:33.130 --> 53:34.131
Oh, God.

53:37.718 --> 53:40.304
Carol, you still there?

53:42.556 --> 53:43.557
You...

53:44.474 --> 53:46.475
You said my life was my own.

53:46.476 --> 53:49.354
It is. One hundred percent.

53:51.231 --> 53:53.275
So, what happens when I say no?

53:54.568 --> 54:00.032
Carol, once you understand
how wonderful this is...

54:01.742 --> 54:02.743
Carol?

54:20.302 --> 54:24.597
Hi! You've reached 505-796-6933.

54:24.598 --> 54:27.308
We're on the French Riviera
drinking champagne.

54:27.309 --> 54:29.936
We are not here in our sweatpants
screening your call.

54:29.937 --> 54:31.146
Make it a good one.

54:32.397 --> 54:34.024
Carol, hello?

54:34.775 --> 54:36.985
It's us. Hello?

54:38.362 --> 54:40.488
We're sorry we upset you, Carol.

54:40.489 --> 54:42.156
We only want to make you happy.

54:42.157 --> 54:44.451
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!
